From 924a71744299491e326b488e5d73d31cb89ae5cb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Clarke <sanity@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Mar 2026 21:09:51 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 14/69] feat(ui,cli): implement any-client contract migration
 on WASM change (#124)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

* feat(ui,cli): implement any-client contract migration on WASM change

When room_contract.wasm changes, the contract key changes, fragmenting
users across different contract instances. Previously only the room
owner could migrate state to the new contract. Now any member can
perform the migration: GET old state → PUT to new key with new WASM.

Changes:
- UI: Any client PUTs state to new contract key (not just owner)
- UI: Follow upgrade pointers in update notifications
- UI: Store previous_contract_key for migration fallback
- CLI: Store previous_contract_key, try GET from old contract for
  fresher state before migrating
- CLI: Follow upgrade pointers in get_room() responses
- Add backwards compatibility rule for ChatRoomStateV1 to AGENTS.md

Related: https://github.com/freenet/river/issues/123

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>

* fix: address review findings for contract migration PR

- Fix compile error: add missing previous_contract_key field in get_response.rs
- Extract duplicate upgrade-pointer-following code into helper function
- Fix "max 5 hops" comment to accurately say "single hop"
- Subscribe to new contract after following upgrade pointer in CLI
- Don't clear previous_contract_key prematurely after WebSocket send;
  instead clear it when GET response confirms migration succeeded

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>

